      "critic": {
        "decision": "accept",
        "reason": "Accept. The patch is a bit-exact refactor of the Q5_0 qh insertion: the multiplier 0x02040810 (2^25+2^18+2^11+2^4) deposits nibble bits b0..b3 into disjoint positions with no carry overlap, and masking with 0x10101010 retains exactly b0->4, b1->12, b2->20, b3->28, identical to the original four shift/mask/or placements for both the low (qh & 0xF) and high ((qh>>16) & 0xF) halves. The hoisted shift vh = qh_word >> 4*iqs combined with qh = vh >> 4*i reproduces the original per-element 4*(iqs+i) shift; for the MMVQ instantiation (vdr=2, iqs in {0,2}) the maximum shift is 12, all consumed bits (0-3, 16-19) are genuine payload with no sign-extension contamination, and no shift exceeds word width. Scope is clean: only vecdotq.cuh at the two declared symbols, matching the manifest, cuda-vecdotq-v1 authority, and the arithmetic change class of akh-v2-q5-type-specific-dequant. No launch geometry or wave count is touched, so no collision with dnr-q5-four-wave or any other DNR fingerprint, and this is distinct from the sealed one-wave continuation. Expected dispatch matches the three sealed true/true anchors with the 129-call false/true tail correctly excluded; cold_serialized load mode is consistent with the fallback-only admission policy. The falsifier (exact type-6 kernel duration under correctness-preserving replay) is well-posed, and the 1139-case MUL_MAT correctness stage gates the impl signature change before any measurement. The mechanism plausibly reduces VALU work (two multiplies plus masks replacing eight shift-mask-or chains per iteration, and elimination of the vh[] register array), which is exactly the type-specific dequant experiment the eligible hypothesis authorizes; whether the multiply latency nets positive is properly left to the governed exact-kernel and graphs-on screens."
      },
